# Keep out of `git archive`, which is how a release reaches the server.
#
# `git archive` does NOT read .dockerignore, so every deploy tarball carried the
# whole repository — 912 MB, of which ~440 MB was data the Docker build discards
# on arrival because .dockerignore already excludes it. Thirteen of those had
# accumulated on cx53: 12 GB to ship the same few megabytes of application.
#
# These paths stay in git and in every clone. `export-ignore` only affects
# archives, so history is untouched and nothing becomes unrecoverable.
#
# Each line below is also in .dockerignore. If you add a path to one, add it to
# the other — they answer the same question ("does the image need this?") for
# two different tools.
originals/      export-ignore
screenshots/    export-ignore
audits/         export-ignore
docs/           export-ignore
tests/          export-ignore
ops/            export-ignore
.claude/        export-ignore
